Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero and let $A$ be a (not necessarily graded) Artinian local $k$-algebra with maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ and Hilbert function $H = (h_0, h_1, \dots, h_j)$, where $h_i = \dim_k \mathfrak{m}^i/\mathfrak{m}^{i+1}$. The generic Jordan type of $A$ is the partition $P(A)$ of $\dim_k A$ giving the Jordan block sizes of multiplication $m_\ell : A \to A$ by a generic linear element $\ell \in \mathfrak{m}$. Several refinements of the Jordan type have been introduced for non-graded Artinian algebras, including:

(a) the sequential Jordan type, recording the Jordan type compatible with the filtration by powers $\mathfrak{m}^i$;
(b) the Loewy sequential Jordan type, recording the Jordan type compatible with the Loewy filtration $0 \subset (0:\mathfrak{m}) \subset (0:\mathfrak{m}^2) \subset \dots \subset A$;
(c) the double sequential Jordan type, combining both filtrations.

Let $Z(H)$ denote the parameter scheme of all Artinian local $k$-algebras with Hilbert function $H$ (viewed inside a suitable punctual Hilbert scheme).

Problem. Exhibit and classify Hilbert function sequences $H$ for non-graded Artinian algebras such that $Z(H)$ has at least two distinct irreducible components $\Xi_1, \Xi_2$ whose general points correspond to algebras sharing the same generic Jordan type but differing in at least one of the refined invariants (sequential Jordan type, Loewy sequential Jordan type, or double sequential Jordan type).

